00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:08.570
On the plus side, the older model features
physical keys instead of the new Touch Bar,

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:09.970
which some prefer.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:17.240
So now let’s get into comparing the MacBook
Air and the MacBook Pro for 2020.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.680
First off, if you’re gonna be buying one
of those Renewed models, keep in mind that

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:25.830
they’re both dual-core models so performance
shouldn’t differ that much, and both of

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.940
them will be a great choice.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:33.050
But if you’re doing any kind of creative
work, I’m talking Photoshop, lightroom,

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:39.390
video editing, programming, working with Logic
Pro, or anything else like that, we fully

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:43.880
recommend going with the 2019 MacBook Pro
with the quad-core processor.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:49.150
That is going to give you so much more performance,
in fact, the base model gives you the best

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:54.731
bang for the buck in terms of processor performance
for the cash, even beating out the 16” MacBook

00:02:54.731 --> 00:02:55.731
Pro.

00:02:55.731 --> 00:02:59.930
Now if you don’t really care much about
performance any you just want a very good

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:05.900
reliable laptop, the MacBook Air is an excellent
choice, and it actually has a few perks over

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:06.900
the Pro.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.450
It’s got 12 hours of battery life instead
of 10 on the Pro.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:15.810
The wedge-shaped design slants the keyboard
downward for a more comfortable typing experience.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:20.280
It’s more portable, weighing a quarter of
a pound less than the Pro.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.430
It gets physical function keys, which a lot
of people like over the Touch Bar.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:29.770
And of course, you also get the gold color
option which you don’t get on the Pro.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:34.390
Now one thing to keep in mind is that both
of these feature the butterfly key switches

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.800
which have had issues in the past.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:41.300
If you want to steer clear of that, we are
expecting new models of these laptops coming

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:46.710
with an updated keyboard possibly some time
this year, but there’s no guarantees.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:53.260
The MacBook Pro, of course, does get a few
perks over the Air, like the larger trackpad

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.430
that’s more convenient.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:04:00.190
It gets a brighter display with better color
accuracy for things like photo and video editing.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:05.330
It gets better quality speakers, and most
importantly, much better performance.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:10.210
So to sum up which MacBook you should buy,
if you do a lot of typing, you need the most

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:14.380
battery life you can get, and you don’t
really care about performance or any type

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.940
of editing or creative work, then the MacBook
Air is going to be perfect for you!

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:24.300
And if you like a bit more of a premium MacBook
with some extra horsepower, better speakers,

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:30.900
better display, and you do any kind of creative
work, 100% absolutely choose the MacBook Pro

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:31.980
over the Air.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:38.301
And if you want the best, most powerful MacBook
ever made, the newly redesigned 16” MacBook

00:04:38.301 --> 00:04:44.090
Pro is a game-changer with incredible amounts
of performance.

